1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,405
Did you know 1 in 3 American adults already has prediabetes, and most don't know it?

2
00:00:04,725 --> 00:00:10,113
Watch for one sign, and two risky habits: skin changes, sitting too much, and skimping on sleep.

3
00:00:10,433 --> 00:00:16,990
Dark, velvety patches on your neck or armpits that won't wash off - that's acanthosis nigricans, a sign of insulin resistance.

4
00:00:17,310 --> 00:00:18,380
Get it checked by a doctor.

5
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:22,308
Sitting eight-plus hours without a break lets insulin resistance build up quietly.

6
00:00:22,628 --> 00:00:27,170
Standing or walking two minutes every half hour can cut after-meal blood sugar by a third.

7
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:33,985
Sleeping less than six hours raises cortisol and blunts insulin sensitivity - linked to roughly a 30% higher diabetes risk.

8
00:00:34,305 --> 00:00:38,149
Protecting seven-plus hours most nights helps insulin do its job again.
